# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Next's metadata image routes emit files with no extension: the cover for a
# post lands at out/blog/<slug>/opengraph-image and is a PNG only by content,
# not by name. Vercel knew the route's type from its build manifest. A static
# host has nothing to go on but the filename, so without these rules it serves
# all 102 of them as application/octet-stream and every Facebook, X and
# LinkedIn card on the site silently fails to render.
#
# The patterns must not overlap. Cloudflare applies every rule that matches and
# joins the values, so listing both /*/opengraph-image and
# /blog/*/opengraph-image produced "content-type: image/png, image/png" on the
# first deploy, which is a malformed header a strict crawler can reject.
# Verified on the live deploy 2026-11-04: `*` spans path separators, so the two
# rules below cover all 102 images between them and nothing matches twice.

/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png

/*/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
